# Example environment file for the PR-review tool.
# Copy this to `.env` and fill in your tokens. `.env` is git-ignored;
# this `.env.example` is a no-secrets template (safe to share).
#
# Provide two GitHub fine-grained Personal Access Tokens, each scoped to your
# target repository (repository permissions only — no account permissions):
#
#   READ-ONLY token (used by the review agent):
#     Metadata: Read, Contents: Read, Pull requests: Read, Issues: Read
#     (no write permission of any kind). Scoping this token read-only is the
#     safety guarantee; pre-flight also verifies it with a live write-isolation
#     probe before any review runs.
GH_TOKEN_READONLY=
#
#   WRITE token (used only by the orchestrator to stage pending reviews):
#     same as read-only, but Pull requests: Read AND write
GH_TOKEN_WRITE=
